hi I'm Angie Rose training manager at  max Renner chocolate bar in New York  City here are ours must try desserts  first off we have our classic European  fondue it comes with three fondues of  your choice we recommend dark chocolate  our house-made toffee and white  chocolate fondue we've got one bowl made  with marshmallows cookies and brownies  the second bowl is pressed fruit  strawberries and bananas so when we  bring it to your table we light a fire  in the grill right in the middle so you  can grab those marshmallows roast them  off to perfection with these three  towers of fondue we have an array of  items for you to dip into it it's  perfect for sharing with all your  friends and family got a little bit of  everything in there to satisfy everyone  Italian thick hot chocolate which is  milk chocolate chunks with steamed milk  whisked down to a nice smooth texture we  then combine that with our house-made  vanilla sauce and while we steam it  the vanilla sauce starts to thicken  creating a velvety texture pouring into  our special maid hug mug it tastes like  a melted chocolate bar in a cup and as  you bring it towards your face with both  your hands giving it a hug it hugs you  back by bringing all the senses of  chocolate into your nose  next up is our s'mores sundae  we start off with some fluffy  marshmallow then some crunchy graham  cracker then we throw in two scoops of  vanilla ice cream two scoops of  chocolate ice cream some warm  peanutbutter sauce drizzled across the  top more of our marshmallow fluff on top  and it's hosted just like your around a  campfire served with white chocolate  fondue and a mounting heap of whipped  cream and another bowl on the side it's  like eating a sundae but it reminds you  of warmth around a campfire when you dig  your spoon from the top to the bottom  you get the crunch from the graham  cracker the smoothness from the peanut  butter followed by some more gooeyness  at the bottom with more marshmallow next  up is the waffle celebration with your  choice of three waffles we make our  waffles in-house we like to recommend  our classic banana split waffle our  brûléed bananas strawberry and cream  waffle mountain of whipped cream last  but certainly not least munchies waffle  but to make it a true celebration we  decided to throw on some sparklers  you'll add a little bit of powdered  sugar and some food Fetty sprinkles this  dish turns heads from the kitchen all  the way to the table this is a really  fun surprise frame  [Music]  last but not least chocolate chunks  pizza we start with our pizza dough milk  chocolate chunks then white chocolate  chunks put it in the oven to melt the  chocolate down so that we can load it up  with tons of mini marshmallows throw it  back in the oven bake it to a golden  brown once it comes out of the oven this  is our classic pizza but we recommend  getting it all fancied up with the works  with warm peanut butter sauce and  caramelized crunchy hazelnut chips so  when we deliver this to our table eyes  light up s'mores on top of pizza can't  come to Max Brenner without having one  of these it's been a favorite of our  guests of all ages for over a decade  [Music]  oh yes  [Music]
 

